I've ascended 3 characters, a V, a W, and an A, all named Angelika.
These were all  between July and November of last year. They all
benefited from early wishes, but my first got only one early wish from
a happy water demon. The A was geno/polyless. Currently, Angelika the
chaotic orcish rogue is attempting a geno/polyless atheist ascension.
She's pretty close, but I haven't had a lot of time to devote to her
recently. I could have ascended her a couple of months ago; she's
being patient, though.

I think my ascensions have been skill fueled by luck. I played off and
on for years before I suddenly started ascending characters. I started
writing detailed notes as I played, and I think that helped a lot. It
helped me focus on what I was doing, and on what plan I should have
given my character's current situation. Paying attention and thinking
before you act is key. But the early wishes definitely helped. Some
day I'll have to try wishless.

